{
  "title": "iOS UI tests: read the diagnostics on the next CI simulator stall",
  "description": "PR #748 added diagnostics to the ios-ui-test-results artifact: logs/runner-load.log (load average, memory pressure and top processes every 15 s) and, on failure only, logs/simulator-system.log.gz (the simulator's system log for the last 40 minutes). \
No iOS UI run had failed since #748 when this was filed. \
When the iOS UI job next fails with kAXErrorIPCTimeout, 'Failed to launch', or 'Timed out while evaluating UI query', check runner-load.log for CPU or memory starvation at the time of the stall, and the SpringBoard and backboardd lines in simulator-system.log.gz, then decide on a targeted fix (for example larger or split jobs if the runner is starved). \
Known CPU users so far: before Spotlight was disabled, mdworker_shared, mds and mds_stores took about 2.5 of the runner's 3 cores; diagnosticd (simulator and host) takes about half a core all the time; and the simulator's mediaanalysisd used 190-380% CPU for the whole UI test run in run 37251142452. scripts/prepare-ios-ui-simulator.sh now unloads mediaanalysisd. \
Check the 'Configure simulator' log and runner-load.log on a few runs to confirm it stays gone; if launchctl remove doesn't work in the simulator, try launchctl bootout or disable. \
The macOS load average stays above 35 on these runners even when idle-ish, so don't gate on it. \
A second kind of stall is not CPU starvation. \
In green run 37252858637, testMealPlanRecipePicker spent about 275 s inside 'Launch com.ramekin.app' while the runner was mostly idle; the 'Failed to launch com.ramekin.app' failure in run 37211763439 is probably the same hang. \
Ruled out: the 'IDELaunchParametersSnapshot ... \
DebuggerVersionStore.StoreError' / 'no debugger version' lines appear on every launch, in fast runs as well as the stalled one (10 times in both 37251142452 and 37252858637), so they don't explain the hang. \
Still open: whether the hang follows the terminate-then-relaunch of the app that XCUIApplication.launch does in every test. \
In green run 37333289156 (PR #761), testLoginFailure, the first test of the run, spent about 290 s between 'Launch com.ramekin.app' and 'Setting up automation session'. \
No earlier app instance existed to terminate, and the app was prebuilt (test-without-building), so the hang is not only a relaunch effect and not tied to building in the same xcodebuild run. \
Separately, a few failures were plain assertion failures rather than stalls: RecipeFlowTests.swift:212 (testRecipeFlow, run 37183180449), :57 (testTextRecipeReviewAndSave, run 36675521178), and 'Sign In must be visible before tapping' (testLoginFailure, run 37175844521). \
Line numbers predate PR #748's test restructuring.",
